# Sage + ACF Project Rules

- **Framework:** Always use Roots Sage (11+).
- **PHP:** Use Laravel-style syntax. Prefer modern PHP (8.x) features.
- **Blade:** Always use Blade components for repetitive HTML. Keep Blade logic minimal.
- **ACF Blocks:**
    - Use Acorn-style data fetching in `app/View/Composers`.
    - Define fields in json files in `app/acf-json/`.
    - Define/Register custom blocks in FISHTANK_BLOCKS in `app/setup.php`
- **Project Structure:**
    - `app/` is for backend logic (Controllers/Composers).
    - `resources/views/` is for frontend templates
    - `resources/styles/` is for general styleing
    - `resources/views/blocks/**/*.scss` for block specific styling
    - `resources/views/blocks/**/*.js` for block specific javascript
    - `resources/views/blocks/text-and-image/` as a rough guide to how we strcture our HTLM and styling
    - `theme.json` used for theme wide settings like colours, spacing, CMS/block functionality etc
- **Constraints:**
    - Always prefer reusable components over large template files.
    - Use `esc_html()` or `esc_attr()` for all user-generated output in PHP.
    - Do not use `get_template_part()`; use `@includeIf` or `<x-component />` syntax.
